name: sngnav_app
description: >-
  Alpha-stage navigation companion for snow-zone commuting. The SPA Actuator
  unit's first edge-developer use of the navigation_safety packages from
  pub.dev — eating our own dog food while learning what fails.
# Build-number discipline (go-live plan GL-A5, 2026-07-20): +N increments per
# Play-track upload; versionCode must never repeat on the track.
version: 0.0.5+2
publish_to: 'none'

environment:
  sdk: ^3.11.1
  flutter: ">=3.41.0"

dependencies:
  flutter:
    sdk: flutter
  # CAP HEALED (measured 2026-07-25 via pub.dev API): the six siblings that
  # once pinned navigation_safety_core ^0.10.0 now ALL admit >=0.10.0 <0.12.0
  # (voice_guidance 0.7.3, navigation_safety 0.9.5, offline_tiles 0.5.4,
  # map_viewport_bloc 0.4.4, driving_conditions 0.5.5, snow_rendering 0.2.8),
  # so navigation_safety_core 0.11.x is now hosted-reachable.
  navigation_safety_core: '>=0.10.0 <0.12.0'
  navigation_safety: ^0.9.0
  voice_guidance: ^0.7.2
  offline_tiles: ^0.5.0
  map_viewport_bloc: ^0.4.0
  driving_conditions: ^0.5.0
  driving_weather: ^0.4.0
  adaptive_reroute: ^0.1.5
  route_condition_forecast: ^0.1.0
  # CAP RELEASED (2026-07-05): route_condition_forecast 0.1.5 widened its
  # routing_engine range, unblocking 0.5.0 — the language-honoring
  # turn-by-turn line (Japanese by default; the instruction the voice lane
  # speaks verbatim). On-device OPS-066 verification still owed before any
  # "reaches HER" claim (docs/on_device_verify_checklist.md).
  routing_engine: ^0.5.0
  fleet_hazard: ^0.5.0
  # ⚠ PINNED BELOW ITS OWN SAFETY RECALL — BLOCKED CATALOG-SIDE, NOT BY CHOICE.
  #
  # snow_rendering 0.3.0 (published 2026-07-26) is a SAFETY RECALL. Verbatim
  # from its CHANGELOG: "Up to and including 0.2.7, this package told drivers
  # 'Conditions normal' about roads it had no data for." The chain was
  #   no data -> RoadSurfaceState.dry -> gripFactor 1.0 (MAXIMUM GRIP)
  #           -> RecommendedResponse.proceed -> "Conditions normal".
  # 0.3.0 fixes it in the type system: fromCondition returns RoadSurfaceState?,
  # and null means "cannot classify" — never dry.
  #
  # ^0.2.0 (= >=0.2.0 <0.3.0) cannot receive it. We TRIED to move; the resolver
  # refused. Measured 2026-08-06 against the live pub.dev API, with the real
  # `flutter pub get` output:
  #
  #   1. snow_rendering >=0.3.0 depends on driving_weather ^0.5.0.
  #      "Because snow_rendering >=0.3.0 depends on driving_weather ^0.5.0 and
  #       sngnav_app depends on driving_weather ^0.4.0, snow_rendering >=0.3.0
  #       is forbidden."
  #   2. Widening driving_weather to ^0.5.0 then fails on a SIBLING:
  #      "Because adaptive_reroute >=0.1.1 depends on driving_weather ^0.4.0
  #       and sngnav_app depends on driving_weather ^0.5.0, adaptive_reroute
  #       >=0.1.1 is forbidden."
  #
  # The complete set of caps, at each package's LATEST PUBLISHED version:
  #   driving_conditions       0.5.5 -> snow_rendering ^0.2.1  AND dw ^0.4.0
  #   adaptive_reroute         0.1.6 -> driving_weather  ^0.4.0
  #   route_condition_forecast 0.1.5 -> driving_weather  ^0.4.0
  # NO published version of ANY sibling admits snow_rendering ^0.3.0.
  #
  # So this is a CATALOG-side blocker, not an app-side one: it clears only when
  # those three are republished admitting driving_weather ^0.5.0 (and
  # driving_conditions admitting snow_rendering ^0.3.0). AAE-3 forbids forcing
  # a constraint past the resolver, and this workspace is fully hosted — no
  # path deps, no dependency_overrides — so no override is used here.
  #
  # Note for whoever does the catalog work: local snow_rendering carries a
  # FURTHER abstention fix (an abstained frost check returning null instead of
  # dry) that is NOT in published 0.3.0, while still labelled `version: 0.3.0`.
  # pub.dev versions are immutable, so that must publish as 0.3.1+.
  #
  # MEANWHILE, the guarantee is enforced at OUR CALL SITE — which is what
  # snow_rendering 0.2.9's own dartdoc instructs: "Never call this with fields
  # you did not measure; gate absence at your call site and tell your user
  # 'unknown'." See lib/services/road_surface_classifier.dart and the pinning
  # test test/services/road_surface_absence_exposure_test.dart.
  snow_rendering: ^0.2.0
  # WIDENED 2026-07-25: ^0.0.3 (= >=0.0.3 <0.0.4) excluded the locked+live
  # 0.0.8, so a clean `pub get` silently DOWNGRADED the aggregator in HER
  # build and `--enforce-lockfile` hard-failed. >=0.0.3 <0.1.0 admits all
  # 0.0.x (measured live 2026-07-25: latest 0.0.8). Same for noaa_nws_adapter.
  # The radiative-frost COVERAGE BOUNDARY — called, never re-derived.
  # humidity_dependent_temperature.dart:123-129 forbids a second copy of this
  # threshold logic by name ("Two independently-maintained copies of this
  # threshold logic ARE that disagreement waiting to happen"), so
  # `radiativeFrostJudgementDeclined` imports the real
  # `computeEffectiveTemperatureCelsius` and the real ceiling constants rather
  # than restating them.
  #
  # A REGULAR dependency, not dev: lib/services/invisible_ice_watch.dart imports
  # it at runtime. It was already resolved TRANSITIVELY at 0.1.3 (via
  # driving_conditions / snow_rendering) and is pinned to that exact version, so
  # promoting it moves no other entry in HER lockfile.
  navigation_safety_calibration: 0.1.3
  condition_aggregator: '>=0.0.3 <0.1.0'
  condition_aggregator_jma: ^0.3.0
  noaa_nws_adapter: '>=0.0.3 <0.1.0'
  flutter_map: ^8.2.2
  flutter_bloc: ^9.0.0
  latlong2: ^0.9.1
  http: ^1.2.0
  intl: ^0.20.2
  geolocator: ^13.0.0
  cupertino_icons: ^1.0.8
# Direct dependency (Tier-1 voice-lane hardening, 2026-07-11): imported by
# lib/actuators/hardened_tts_engine.dart (awaitSpeakCompletion + nav audio
# attributes + focus-duck + read-the-1/0-result) and
# lib/services/voice_lane_readiness.dart (getVoices ja/network_required
# read). Also floor-pins the version so a voice_guidance range change can
# never silently downgrade HER voice lane.
# Maintainer watch (FEM 2026-07-11): flutter_tts idle since 2026-01; if it
# breaks on a future targetSdk, the lane is fork-or-vendor via voice_guidance.
  flutter_tts: ^4.2.5
  # NOTE: the bundled ja safety audio deliberately has NO third-party player.
  # `audioplayers` was tried and REMOVED: audioplayers_android 5.3.0 (the latest)
  # ships a buildscript pinned to Kotlin 1.7.10 / AGP 7.3.1 and a top-level
  # `kotlin {}` block for a plugin it never applies, which cannot resolve under
  # Flutter's modern plugin-loader — it BROKE `flutter build apk` outright while
  # `flutter test` stayed green, because the tests never build an APK. A safety
  # voice may not sit on a Gradle contract that can silently un-build the app.
  # The mouth is first-party: android/.../MainActivity.kt + MediaPlayer, one file.
  vibration: ^3.2.0
  wakelock_plus: ^1.6.1
  navigation_safety_enums: ^0.1.4
  flutter_localizations:
    sdk: flutter
  compound_failure_advisor: ^0.1.1
  localization_fallback: ^0.1.1
  # Offline-basemap PoC wiring (Chair Option A, 2026-07-01): read the bundled
  # placeholder MBTiles archive + write it to a temp file for sqlite3 to open.
  # Both are already transitively present via offline_tiles; declared directly
  # so app code may import them (depend_on_referenced_packages).
  mbtiles: ^0.5.0
  path_provider: ^2.1.5
  # Bundles libsqlite3.so on Android/iOS. WITHOUT this, package:sqlite3
  # cannot open the bundled MBTiles on a real device (Android forbids
  # loading the system libsqlite3), MbTiles() throws, and the offline
  # basemap silently fell back to network tiles — the map was BLANK in
  # airplane mode on-device while every host-side test painted it.
  # Caught by the 2026-07-10 emulator airplane-mode pass.
  # DO NOT bump past 0.5.x without an on-device airplane-mode re-verify:
  # 0.6.0+eol is a deprecated NO-OP (the .so moves to package:sqlite3 build
  # hooks, which did NOT deliver on our 2026-07-10 build). ^0.5.24 cannot
  # float to 0.6.0 (caret-on-0.x), so only a manual bump can re-open the
  # blank-offline-map failure. FEM ecosystem read 2026-07-11.
  sqlite3_flutter_libs: ^0.5.24
  # C6 ログを共有 — user-initiated share-sheet export of the local error
  # log (text share; no FileProvider, no manifest change).
  share_plus: ^13.2.0

dev_dependencies:
  flutter_test:
    sdk: flutter
  flutter_lints: ^6.0.0
  # Direct sqlite reads in the offline-archive contract test (per-zoom tile
  # counts + custom metadata keys the mbtiles API does not expose).
  sqlite3: ^3.3.4

flutter:
  uses-material-design: true
  assets:
    # REAL offline Akita basemap — OpenStreetMap cartography (minimal style):
    # Akita prefecture z8-z12; z13 at Akita city + prefecture-wide selective
    # rural tiles (major road or town, clipped to the 秋田県 boundary). Sea
    # fill, network-verified route shields (国道/県道/expressway), bridge/
    # tunnel styling, lakes incl. multipolygon relations, ja labels, honest
    # no-data tint. Pipeline + runbook: tool/README_TILES.md (cut pinned
    # tohoku-260709). Data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.
    - assets/tiles/akita_offline.mbtiles
    # The offline MOUTH — the finite ja safety vocabulary, pre-rendered to WAV
    # (open_jtalk / nitech-jp, 16 kHz mono). The system TTS is silent and then
    # hangs with no network on the target device, so every warning the app had
    # hardened arrived at a layer that could not speak it. These bytes ship in
    # the APK: no network, no voice-pack download, no TTS engine required.
    # Source of truth: lib/voice/offline_safety_voice.dart
    # Re-render:      bash tool/render_offline_voice.sh
    - assets/audio/ja/
    # Font attribution rides in the APK beside the font it licenses
    # (Bitstream Vera license requires the notice to accompany copies).
    - assets/fonts/LICENSE-SnGNavSymbols.txt
  fonts:
    # SnGNavSymbols — a 14-glyph symbols subset (⚠ ❄ → ※ ° … et al.) cut
    # from DejaVu Sans and renamed per its license's modification clause
    # (assets/fonts/LICENSE-SnGNavSymbols.txt). Bundled because the ja
    # system font stack does NOT guarantee these glyphs (measured
    # 2026-07-30: Noto Sans CJK JP lacks U+2744 ❄; harness fonts lack
    # U+26A0 ⚠ — the 1b reach-class tofu defect, plan 2026-07-25 §1).
    # Wired as app-wide ThemeData.fontFamilyFallback in main.dart; glyph
    # coverage is drift-guarded by test/fonts/symbol_font_coverage_test.dart
    # (a new symbol in a lib/ string literal fails the suite until the
    # subset is re-cut — tool/subset_symbols_font.md documents the re-cut).
    - family: SnGNavSymbols
      fonts:
        - asset: assets/fonts/SnGNavSymbols.ttf
